; A basket price's commodities are written into its value expression in
; commodity order, so the expression text is the same on every run.
;
; A P directive whose parenthesized price evaluates to several commodities
; (#1101) gives the commodity a value expression rebuilt from that
; balance's components.  Postings of the commodity carry it as a lot
; annotation, so the text shows in print, --lots reports, emacs output and
; -V errors.  Ledger used to write the components in the order in which
; the balance happened to keep them: USD before EUR for bicur (1101.test's
; basket), and CAD last for tricur.  That order changes from run to run,
; so the text is written in commodity order instead: CAD, EUR, USD for
; tricur, where the directive has EUR, CAD, USD.

P 2015-01-01 bicur (EUR 0.45 + USD 0.55)
P 2015-01-01 tricur (EUR 0.40 + CAD 0.25 + USD 0.35)

2015/01/01 Baskets
    Assets:Basket    1 bicur
    Assets:Basket    1 tricur
    Equity

test print
2015/01/01 Baskets
    Assets:Basket                       1 bicur ((({EUR 0.45} + {USD 0.55})))
    Assets:Basket                       1 tricur (((({CAD 0.25} + {EUR 0.40}) + {USD 0.35})))
    Equity
end test
